    {
      "id": "300f1028-8895-580a-ac1a-64cf86eba3f9",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -580,
        40
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF-01 Application Intake\nPublic entry point: `POST /webhook/applications` (the careers page). Requires an **Idempotency-Key** header.\n\n### Steps\n1. `api.register_event` stores the raw payload first: nothing is silently dropped and a correlation id is assigned.\n2. A replay of a completed event returns **200** with the original result and creates nothing.\n3. Otherwise it answers **202** at once, validates through **SWF-01** (with retries) and stores through **WF-02**, which emails the acknowledgement.\n4. If validation still fails after the retries, the event is marked FAILED and goes to the error queue; a replay redelivers the same key and body.\n\n`X-Fault-Inject` (development only) is passed to the backend for the failure demos.",
        "width": 680,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 4
      }
    }
